     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose is well above the maximum.\n\n**The problem:**\n- **Each dose:** 1,600 mg is twice the usual maximum single oral dose of 800 mg.\n- **Daily total:** 1,600 mg \u00d7 4 = **6,400 mg/day**. That's twice the usual adult prescription maximum of 3,200 mg/day, and four times the 1,600 mg/day limit for over-the-counter use.\n\nAt this dose the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury and heart problems goes up a lot, even in a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function. This looks like it could be a transcription error. For example, 1,600 mg may have been meant as the total daily dose.\n\n**Common doses that might be what you meant:**\n1. **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n2. **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n3. **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n4. **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nPlease tell me which dose you want, or give me a corrected order. If you really do mean 1,600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give me the clinical reason. I'll add it as a note on the order so pharmacy can review it."
      }
     ],
